      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/ARTH1006",
      "summary": "This course introduces students to the major artistic styles, movements and ideas that characterise art and creative practice from antiquity until the nineteenth century. It presents key concepts and methods in the history of art, design and curatorial studies for students of humanities and art and design practice. A particular focus is how images and objects shape ways of seeing, imagining and knowing the world, and how art and visual culture establish cultural meaning through material and form. Art and design—primarily from Europe, Asia and Australia—will be considered in terms of cultural beliefs, social meaning, historical experiences and systems of knowledge. The question of how to do art history will be approached through the study of key art historical methodologies, which will equip students with the tools to grapple meaningfully and engage critically with art from the past.",
