      "summary": "This course introduces students to aspects of the fascinating realm of popular culture in East Asia. Students learn about major theoretical paradigms in cultural studies, and how they may apply to developments in East Asian popular culture in the past and present. Emphasis is placed on what drives the consumption of popular culture, and whether that consumption can be argued to represent resistance. Case studies are drawn from, among others, advertising, cinema, toys, comics, gadgets, fashion, pop music, sports, and social media in mainland China, Taiwan, Japan, and North and South Korea, with a slight emphasis on the latter.",
