      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/BIOL6194",
      "summary": "This course is designed to provide an opportunity for students to learn about applications of biological sciences in a broad range of workplaces and to get exposure to the contemporary employment landscape. Various guest speakers, who will be professionals in different areas of biological science and/or research, will discuss their work, career, ethics and legal liability as well as what they see as emerging career opportunities in their fields. Visits to work places will be organised. Students will also work in small groups workshops including informational interviews and careers workshops, designed to promote confidence and develop skills for job searches and when transitioning to the workforce. Enrolment places are limited to 70 and students will be selected on a first-come, first serve basis. Please go to https://students.science.anu.edu.au/program-admin/requesting-permission-enrol to request a permission code to enrol in this course. This course is assessed on a Course Requirement Satisfied (CRS) or Fail basis.",
