      "summary": "This course builds on the skills acquired in Burmese 1001 and continues the study of spoken-style Burmese in both oral and written forms. Students will expand their vocabulary, develop greater grammatical accuracy, and learn to express abilities, experiences, and comparisons. Instruction emphasizes both language skills and socio-cultural awareness, enabling students to engage with everyday conversations and read simple passages in Burmese script. Course topics include the education system, part-time job interviews, Myanmar’s geography and ethnic diversity, traditional festivals, and the contrasts between urban and rural life. Authentic materials and cultural content provide meaningful contexts for communication, while guest speakers—Burmese native speakers and Myanmar specialists—offer students exposure to authentic language and cultural perspectives. By the end of the course, students will have strengthened their receptive, interactive, and productive skills, gaining greater confidence in both spoken and written Burmese.",
