      "summary": "This course builds on skills learned in Burmese 3 and provides students with extensive opportunities to review, practice, and expand their knowledge of spoken-style Burmese. The course content enables students to access authentic Burmese materials across both print and online platforms, including newspapers, magazine articles, governmental documents, short stories, poems, and excerpts from literary works. A rich variety of listening comprehension materials, including news, podcasts, and engaging discussions on academic topics, will enhance the development of students' speaking skills. Fascinating topics include Myanmar history, economics, anthropology, mythology, and practical conversations such as negotiations and problem-solving in business/academic contexts. These diverse topics significantly deepen students' understanding of Myanmar culture and society. Students will create Burmese compositions and speech scripts in spoken-style Burmese on both assigned topics and self-selected research topics of their interest related to Myanmar. The course regularly features Burmese native speakers and Myanmar specialists as guest speakers to enhance students' speaking abilities and provide authentic language exposure. Students will deliver presentations to these guests based on the topics covered throughout the course, creating valuable real-world communication experiences.",
