      "summary": "This course examines normative, positive and critical theories of accounting and their influence on contemporary practice. It explores the conceptual framework, major historical and current debates, and the role of theory in shaping accounting standards, reporting practices and the use of financial information. Emphasis is placed on real-world application, highlighting how different perspectives affect the decisions of managers, investors, regulators and other stakeholders. By linking theory to practice, the course provides students with a deeper understanding of accounting’s foundations and its impact on business and society, supporting both professional careers and further study in accounting.",
