      "summary": "Modern Chinese 1: Written (CHIN1013) is designed for absolute beginners who are (near-) native speakers of English. It introduces the basics of the Standard Modern Chinese language such as sounds and tones, the pinyin system (Chinese Romanization), vocabulary, and simple sentence structures associated with a range of communicative expressions. The course provides intensive training on literacy skills. Handwritten and/or computer-typing simplified characters are taught and practised throughout the course to develop students’ elementary reading and writing capacities. Pinyin is introduced at the beginning of the course and will be used as an assisting phonetic tool in this course. Students are expected to complete assessments mainly using Chinese characters unless otherwise instructed in a specific assessment item. This course shares the textbook and one weekly lecture with Modern Chinese 1: Spoken (CHIN1012) and has another more specialised weekly lecture on its own. Each shared lecture (Lecture A) gives an overview of the weekly lesson in the textbook. It then focuses on introducing the main grammar points and sentence structures of the week.",
