      "summary": "Algorithms are the foundation of Computer Science. They enable advances in Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Cybersecurity, Distributed, Mobile, and Cloud Computing, Computer Graphics and Animation, and many more. These advances have made Computer Science an indispensable part of our everyday life. The main goal of this course is to familiarize students with basic concepts in the design and analysis of algorithms and data structures. It focuses on fundamental computing problems such as sorting and searching. The students will learn how to use different algorithm design methods and data structures to solve such problems efficiently, as well as basic performance measures and analysis techniques.",
