      "summary": "This course covers competition policy and a brief introduction to the economics of regulation. We use theoretical industrial organisation models to analyse firms' competitive and anti-competitive behaviour . We will study conducts such as collusion, merger, vertical control, predation, and some other non-price monopolization practices. We will also discuss various competition policy guidelines including the ACCC merger guideline and Competition and Consumer Act 2010. In the last part of the course, we briefly introduce the theory of regulation.",
