      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/EMDV8017",
      "summary": "Pollution and waste now pose significant risks to nature and our built environments, with important consequences for health and well-being. This course examines the causes, implications and governance of environmental pollution and waste. Informed by work on environmental justice, risk, and science and technology studies, the course uses a series of case studies to investigate how we understand pollution and waste in their different forms; individual, societal and intergovernmental responses to pollution and waste; and policy options and their limitations in governing these issues. The case studies will vary from year to year, but will draw on examples from the identified themes of industry, urban environments, legacy pollutants (e.g. mercury), plastics, and pollution emergencies (e.g. oil spills).",
