      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/EMSC6123",
      "summary": "Do you want to learn how to recognise and interpret rocks in the field and laboratory? In this course you will learn about basic geological concepts around the formation, evolution and deformation of rocks and geological structures in the solid earth. The material learned in this course will give you the background needed to tackle the big questions facing our planet in subsequent courses. It will be divided into three sections; (i) sedimentology (ii) geological structures and (iii) igneous and metamorphic petrology. Part (i) deals with the formation of sedimentary rocks over a variety of depositional environments. Part (ii) is concerned with recognition and interpretation of basic geological structures such as faults and folds. Part (iii) covers the formation of magmas, igneous rocks and rock-forming silicate minerals, and the mineralogy and textures of metamorphic rocks. This course is co-taught with undergraduate students but assessed separately.",
