      "summary": "This course investigates the intertwined relationship between writing and technology. From the Gutenberg Press to ChatGPT, technology has always had a profound impact on how we write, what we write, and how writing is circulated and read. This course introduces theoretical conceptions of publishing, authorship, and textuality. These concepts lay the foundations for understanding important contemporary debates about the impact of technology on writing and literature. This includes crucial discussions of authenticity, originality, commercialisation, and platformisation. Students will apply these theories and develop a deeper understanding of these debates through analysis of new digital forms of writing, and literary works that engage deeply with the relationship between writing and old and new technologies.",
