      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/ENVS2004",
      "summary": "Australia is a country underpinned by a variable climate that influences virtually every aspect of our lives. So what makes Australia the ‘land of drought and flooding rains’? What are the factors that influence major fires, heatwaves and droughts that have shaped Australian society? How is climate change influencing Australian climate variability and extremes? What applications does weather and climate have in sectors such as the urban environment, human health, energy resources and science communication? In this course we provide a foundation for understanding Australian weather and the application of this knowledge to other societal impacting weather phenomenon. It is designed to lead students into advanced third year courses in climatology, climate change, bushfire science, and climate change policy. It is also provides a multidisciplinary understanding of climate for students pursuing ecology, environmental science, natural resource management, or sustainability studies.",
