      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/ENVS3042",
      "summary": "This course will introduce students to advanced concepts associated with agri-food system innovation and adaptation. This course will build on understanding gained in ENVS2023 and ENVS6223 and explore how innovation and adaptation: can identify future opportunities and mitigate threats or productivity declines in agri-food systems;can alter existing trajectories away from commodity-specific and incremental change, towards transformational change;can ensure that a more balanced approach to delivering agri-food system outcomes is achieved, that considers multiple outcomes e.g. economic, environmental and social;must operate in tandem with an improved regulatory environment in order to achieve sustained agri-food system outcomes. The course is intended to provide students the knowledge and skills to be able to identify where disruptions may occur in existing agri-food systems and formulate technical and policy-based adaptation options that will serve to mitigate these disruptions.",
