      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/HCAI9002",
      "summary": "This course will facilitate the writing and submission of a journal article, based on an existing draft piece of writing such as a thesis chapter or conference paper. Through a series of discussions, exercises and activities, including peer review of drafts, students will learn to structure a journal article, position their article in relation to current research, distill a cogent and compelling argument with sufficient evidence, and find an appropriate journal. As part of the course, students will become familiar with the peer review and publishing processes used by scholarly journals, and will critically examine scholarship on academic writing and publishing.",
