      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/INTR2024",
      "summary": "In this course we will study the politics of the possession, management, and control of the most destructive weapon ever created. We will analyse the history and current policies of the states that possess nuclear weapons, as well as “threshold” states that maintain some ability to acquire a nuclear capability. We will examine the attempts to control the spread of these weapons, successful and otherwise, and even examples of states giving up nuclear capabilities. The course will also explore contemporary trends in technological developments that have an impact on nuclear balances, the links between the civilian nuclear industry and weapons programmes, and the illicit or ‘blackmarket’ trade in nuclear materials.",
