      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/LAWS4225",
      "summary": "This course aims to provide students with a critical understanding of international human rights law and practice. Topics to be covered include: historical development of international human rights law;international humanitarian law (the law of armed conflict) and its relationship with the international law of human rights;human rights ‘enforcement' mechanisms: the UN Human Rights Council, the human rights treaty bodies and human rights regional mechanisms;the rights of women and the rights of indigenous peoples;threats to rights, particularly counter-terrorism measures;application of international human rights law in Australia, including refugee issues; andthe future development of rights, including collective rights and lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender and intersex (LGBT) rights.",
