      "summary": "This course examines labour law in Australia. Labour law is an important component of studies in the legal regulation of commerce. Students are introduced to the key aspects of labour laws which determine the rights, entitlements and responsibilities of employers and workers in the workplace. Both practical and theoretical perspectives on judge-made law and statute regulating work are examined. Given extensive recent legislative activity by the Commonwealth Parliament in the area of labour law, the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) as amended is analysed in some detail. Topics covered include: the history, development and constitutional underpinnings of Australian labour lawemployees contrasted with other categories of workersthe common law contract of employmentminimum employment terms and conditionsworkplace bargaining and agreementsthe regulation of industrial conflict (including strikes)wrongful, unlawful and unfair termination of employment.",
