      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/LAWS4236",
      "summary": "This course examines the law governing succession of property after the death of the owner. Major topics include: the nature of wills;capacity to make a will, intention to make a will, undue influence, formalities for making a will and how a will is revoked and altered;the interpretation of wills;the administration of deceased estates;how an estate is divided when there is no will; andhow the law protects family members against being disinherited through a will.The course concentrates on the law of New South Wales and the ACT. Occasionally, comparisons are made to the law of other Australian jurisdictions. To develop their knowledge and skills, students will complete readings, engage in independent research of a variety of materials and databases and provide legal advice on matters covered in the course.",
