      "summary": "This course examines important facets of the regulation of corporations. It investigates the law and policy relating to the acquisition of control of corporations, particularly by takeover, and the regulation of financial markets generally. Topics to be covered may include: issues prompting, and theories shaping, the regulation of takeovers and the securities industry generally; the regulation of financial markets; the powers of the Australian Securities and Investment Commission and the obligations of listed companies, brokers and dealers; controls upon market manipulation and insider trading; the legal requirements for prospectuses; controls upon the acquisition of shares under Chapter 6 of the Corporations Act 2001 (Cth); directors' responsibilities in a takeover situation; and compulsory acquisition powers. To develop their knowledge and skills, students will engage in a range of learning activities, including seminars and collaborative group work.",
