      "summary": "International Humanitarian Law seeks to limit the effects of war and armed conflict and provides protection for individuals. The course examines the history of international humanitarian law, the relevant international conventions – especially the Geneva Conventions and the Additional Protocols – and current issues that have emerged as a result of the application and interpretation of IHL in recent conflicts. Topics covered may include conflicts and applicable law, protected persons, conduct of hostilities, weapons, addressing violations of the law, and deep dives into current events. To develop their knowledge and skills, students will engage in interactive classes incorporating lectures, guest lecturers and collaborative learning to operationalise the law through, for example, role play and simulations.",
