      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/LAWS8445",
      "summary": "The course looks at the intersection of Information Technology and Law. Five broad subject areas are identified and explored within this intersection from the impact of digital content, through to the challenges and opportunities of a vastly interconnected, perhaps \"borderless\" society. Anyone who was intrigued by the movie \"The Social Network\" will be interested in this course. The areas of study are: information technology and intellectual property; censorship; privacy; computer crime and evidence; and e-commerce and IT contracts. An important component of the course is the cultivation of an understanding of the underlying technology. To develop their knowledge and skills in this emerging area of law, students will engage in a range of learning activities, including seminars, undertaking self-directed, expert-supported research and engaging with research materials.",
