      "summary": "This course looks to critical approaches to international law, with focus on approaches from developing countries and indigenous peoples. Third World Approaches to International Law (TWAIL) refers to the thoughts of developing countries regarding international law. Fourth World Approaches to International Law (FWAIL) refers to the concerns of indigenous peoples regarding international law. The course is intended to give students an introduction to both bodies of literature, with a broad overview of the major concerns, critiques, principles, issues, and applications of both. The course covers theory, policy, & practice, with attention to ongoing controversies and challenges in implementation.",
