      "summary": "This course is the fourth and final year of the four-year Doctor of Medicine and Surgery (MCHD) program. MEDI8304 comprises an elective block, four clinical rotation blocks (Women's Health and Newborn Care, Psychiatry and Addiction Medicine, Senior Medicine and Surgery and Acute Care) and a common final PRINT (Pre-Internship) block. The MEDI8304 blocks are designed to consolidate clinical reasoning and practical skills through immersion within a range of clinical environments. The emphasis throughout each block is on self-directed, experiential learning and deep involvement in the day-to-day care of patients. Students will have clear requirements for attendance, patient clerking and unit involvement. The attachments allow students to consolidate their intern readiness skills and participate in the management of their patients. Elements of Population Health, Professionalism and Leadership, Evidence Based Practice, Research and Clinical Skills are integrated throughout the course. Course Structure and Content Four clinical rotations blocks: Senior Medicine and Surgery Acute Care Psychiatry and Addiction Medicine Women's Health and Newborn Care Pre Internship (PRINT) block Each student will have an individual timetable and unique placement sequence. MEDI8303 and MEDI8304 form Phase 2 of the MCHD program.",
