      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/PHIL2150",
      "summary": "This course is an introduction to formal logic for students with no prior familiarity with the subject. Logic is the study of validity, a property of good arguments. In formal logic we approach this in a mathematical way, introducing a formal (symbolic) language and using this to study logical properties like logical consequence and logical equivalence. This course begins with truth-function operators and truth-tables, and by the end we have learned a proof-system for first-order logic and established its soundness and completeness. The coursework will include regular problem sets.",
