      "summary": "This course introduces students to the microscopic theory of matter and radiation that spans elementary particles to atoms. Building upon prior learning in quantum mechanics and electromagnetism, students will develop understanding of the standard model of particle physics, and the formation and structure of nuclei and atoms. As a result, students will be able to interpret the universe that surrounds them in terms of its most fundamental constituents and apply this knowledge to advances in fundamental physics, radiation safety and medical science, nuclear power, atomic technologies (eg. lasers, atomic clocks, MRI) and quantum chemistry.",
