      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/PSYC9002P",
      "summary": "As a PhD candidate, you will work with increased independence, under the direction of a supervisory panel of experts in the field. Your research will make an original and important contribution to human knowledge, research and development. This program is designed for those who have a particular interest in the academic and research aspects of clinical psychology. Graduates of this program have the benefit of the training provided to Master of Clinical Psychology candidates with the intensive research training provided by completing a research PhD in the field of clinical psychology. The PhD (Clinical Psychology) program aims to develop effective clinical competencies and to encourage a critical approach to the application of these competencies to practice. The emphasis is on a science-based approach to clinical psychology and the development of clinical problem solving skills, with a focus on scientific evidence combined with practical experience based on the theory of clinical psychology. Please view the website for further information on the program, environment and resources offered by the School of Medicine and Psychology .",
