      "summary": "Students will continue their clinical work by beginning a placement external to the ANU Psychology Clinic. External placements are in a wide range of settings external to the Clinic and students must complete two external placements (Placement Ill and Placement IV). The external placement is normally 40 days in duration, at a rate of 2 or 3 days a week for approximately 4 to 5 months. In addition to the placement, students are required to attend Professional Ethics and Practice meetings once a week for one hour during the teaching semester. Psychology placements provide students with opportunities to: (a) observe practice by qualified professionals; (b) apply, under supervision, the knowledge and skills they have acquired in assessment, formulation, intervention, evaluation and reporting; (c) receive feedback on their performance; and, (d) to gain experience in the planning and organisation of services. Students must undertake at least 1000 hours of supervised practical experience spread over four placements. This includes 400 hours of direct client contact.",
