      "handbookUrl": "https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/course/THAI1002",
      "summary": "This course introduces students to spoken and written Thai, the language spoken in Thailand and by the Thai diaspora worldwide. It is appropriate for students without any background in Thai language. Students will learn the tones, consonants, vowels, essential grammar, and the writing system of the Thai language. They are the building blocks of students' reading, writing, listening, and speaking skills. Students will learn, practise, and employ a range of simple sentence structures with appropriate polite particles through a series of situational dialogues. The language use and topics cover greetings and self-introduction, giving basic information on self, family and friends, time and date, description of objects, and asking for help, information and directions. Cultural issues involved language use and politeness will be included. The course also covers basic knowledge of Thailand. By the end of the course, students will be able to read and write basic Thai sentences and use the language in simple day-to-day communication and situations. This course will prepare students for the second course of Thai.",
