      "summary": "Thai 2 continues from Thai 1. In this course, students further develop their communicative, receptive, and productive skills of Thai. This course covers the topics of travelling and transportation, leisure activities, invitations, going to see a doctor, and Thai ways of life and festivities. Students will expand their grammatical use of more complex conjunctions, comparison, tenses indicators, and passive voice. Students will practise various skills through conversation on topics covered in class, translation exercises, and increased Thai language exposure through audio-visual media. Cultural issues in relation to language, cultural practice in daily life, and customs will also be included. By the end of the course, students will be able use a wider range of commonplace grammatical structures and communicate in a broader range of day-to-day situations.",
